course: dictionary
lesson: 5297
title: Many meanings of just
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Just» is a small word with many meanings, so the words around it are your clues. Ask yourself: does it mean only, exactly, a moment ago, barely, or fair?
explain: «Rights are things every person should have just for being human.» The words for being human tell you that just means only, or simply because. Try the swap: «for being human only» still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Some children are adopted, and they are just as much part of the family.» Here just means exactly: the same amount, not more and not less. «He has just left» is different. It means a very short time ago, so the clue is the word has.
explain: The formal words are merely, precisely, solely and equitable. Stories also use just to mean fair: «a just ruler is fair to everyone.» When you are not sure, read the sentence again and try your meaning.
fact: «Just» can mean exactly, only, a very short time ago, barely, or fair.
fact: «Just 3 dollars» means only 3 dollars, and «just one more» means only one more.
fact: «He has just left» means he left a very short time ago.
fact: «Just in time» means only just in time, or barely on time.
fact: «A just king» means a fair and right king; formal words for this are equitable and fair.
exercise: «He has just left the room.» What does just mean here? | Only | Fair | Exactly, to the second | *A very short time ago
exercise: «Rights are things every person should have just for being human.» What does just mean here? | Fair | *Only, simply because | Very fast | Exactly in time
exercise: «She was just in time for the bus.» What does just mean here? | Fair and right | A very long time ago | *Only just, barely | Exactly the same
test: «A just ruler is fair to everyone.» What does just mean? | Very quickly | Barely | Only | *Fair and right
test: «The shop sold just 3 apples.» What does just mean? | Exactly | Fairly | Very fast | *Only
exam: «A just king» uses just as a formal word; which word is the best formal swap for just here? | Precisely | Merely | Solely | *Equitable
